#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# out

#% text
# `out(n)` gives the value of numbered statement `n` of a notebook session; `out()` gives the last value, and `out(-k)` the `k`-th previous one.
# In a notebook, `%`, `%%` and `%n` are short for `out(-1)`, `out(-2)` and `out(n)`.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# Statements are numbered across the cells of a notebook; scripts and the REPL do not number statements.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
x0 = 2^10
out(-1) + 1
#% output
#= 1025

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `timing`, `eval`
